  "context_pill": "Section 36(1)(iva)",
  "example_summary": "Computation of deduction u/s 36(1)(iva) and disallowance for X Ltd. contributing to a pension scheme.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Section 36(1)(iva) & Section 43B\n\n| Statutory Head / Section | Core Condition & Threshold | Permissible Deduction / Disallowance Rule |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 36(1)(iva)** | Contribution by employer to a notified pension scheme under Section 80CCD. | Restricted to **14% of salary** of the employee for the relevant previous year. |\n| **Salary Definition** | Includes **Basic Salary** plus **Dearness Allowance**, provided DA forms part of retirement benefits (pay). | Any employer contribution exceeding **14% of salary** is disallowed under PGBP. |\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Statutory Cap Rule: Under Section 36(1)(iva), if the employer contributes more than 14% of the employee's salary towards a notified pension scheme, the excess contribution is strictly disallowed as a business expense under Section 36(1)(iva).\n\n> [!NOTE] Definition of Salary: Salary for computing the 14% limit specifically comprises Basic Salary and Dearness Allowance, but only if Dearness Allowance forms part of the pay under the terms of employment.",
